<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel">
      <p xml:id="Aink157-kilavi">
        parattaiyiṟpirintu vāyilvēṇṭi oḻukukiṉṟa talaimakaṉ putalvaṉ vāyilāka varumeṉakkēṭṭu añciya talaimakaḷ putalvaṉ viḷaiyāṭit taṉittuvantuḻic colliyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
        Spoken by the heroine who was afraid, having heard of the hero wanting to enter [after] separating from the other woman; [in relief] when [her] son, having gone to play, returned alone [= without the father].
  </p>
</div>    
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink157">
<l>veḷḷāṅ kurukiṉ piḷḷai cetteṉak</l>
<l>kāṇiya ceṉṟa maṭanaṭai nārai</l>
<l>kālai yiruntu mālaic cēkkun</l>
<l>teṇkaṭaṟ cērppaṉoṭu vārāṉ</l>
<l>ṟāṉvan taṉaṉeṅ kāta lōṉē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
       <l> He, my lover,</l>
        <l>Did not come with the man of the shore with clear waters</l>
        <l>In which the wader with an inexperienced walk that went to see,</l>
        <l>since the hatchling of the white wader died,</l>
       <l>Rests in the evening, having sat [there] in the daytime.</l>
        <l>[That man from the shore] came alone.</l>
      </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
